{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZ5bP2pXgNUdV1thRFt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zest's new restaurant concierge is reached by texting a phone number, and the company is treating that as its main interface going forward. TechCrunch describes the launch as part of a broader shift in which startups let conversational AI agents handle tasks that used to require opening a stand-alone mobile app, and it compares the concierge to agents like Instinct and Poke. CEO Mario Gomez-Hall puts it directly: \"The agent is the product now.\"\n\nFor a company this size, the change carries real weight. Zest was founded in November 2024, raised $1.8 million in pre-seed funding from Alexis Ohanian at 776 and Steve Jang at Kindred Ventures, and has an initial base of thousands of users. By moving to text, it hopes to scale beyond that base and start generating revenue, with booking and food ordering as the first revenue lines.\n\nThe group chat feature shows where a text interface changes the task. Zest can be dropped into an existing thread, blend everyone's tastes, run a vote, and book a table for the group. It seems likely that this is easier to do where people are already discussing the plan than in a separate app, though that is an inference and the article does not report usage numbers for it.\n\nWhether a text concierge draws more users than the app did is not yet established. The article reports the strategy and one publication's positive tests, not adoption results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":810,"cache_read_input_tokens":5501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":810},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nu